id:                     E369
trigger_tool: sh|mv|binary-sign-tool|runtime
phase: testing|runtime|cleanup
error_signature: signed execution root publication identity|foreign replacement preserved during cleanup|mv -n.*existing directory|signing transaction cleanup incomplete|identity changed during acquisition|signing transaction interrupted by TERM
severity: 2
category: transactional-elf-signing
match_keywords: ELF signing, binary-sign-tool, signed-exec.pending, cleanup ownership, mv -nT, no-clobber, path replacement, signal deferral, held FD, coherent commit, device inode
title: Identity-bound acquisition and coherent publication for signed execution trees
root_cause: A global cleanup flag cannot prove ownership of individual paths; create, inode capture, and owner publication can also be interrupted before cleanup authority becomes visible, independent final flags can split root/evidence commit, and mv -n without -T can move pending state inside a foreign directory.
affected_scope: Shell-based target runners that sign task-private ELF copies, publish a directory or evidence file, and clean incomplete work after failure or HUP/INT/TERM.
verification_cmd: Run the production runner through pending/transition stat-failure, replacement and deferred-TERM acquisition cases, final/evidence replacement, TERM immediately before and after the single commit assignment; require 23/23 and fixture cleanup back to the pre-state.
rec_priority: 1
rec_approach: per-object-identity-bound-no-clobber-publication
rec_description: Hold acquisition objects by FD, defer and replay signals until identity-bound ownership is visible, publish with mv -nT, establish destination ownership before releasing source ownership, and use one committed state so root and evidence are cleaned or preserved as a pair.
rec_command: stat -c '%d:%i' "/proc/$owner_pid/fd/$fd" && mv -nT "$pending" "$final" && test "$(stat -c '%d:%i' "$final")" = "$held_identity"
rec_auto_fix: false
rec_impl: manual
fallback_priority: 2
fallback_approach: target-local-rename-noreplace-helper
fallback_description: When the frozen target mv lacks -T or no-clobber semantics, use a hash-bound task-local helper that exposes renameat2 RENAME_NOREPLACE and validates the moved object identity before cleanup authority transfer.
fallback_command:
fallback_auto_fix: false
fallback_impl: manual
forbid_1_pattern: SIGNING_TRANSACTION_ACTIVE.*rm -rf|global cleanup flag
forbid_1_reason: One transaction-wide flag does not prove that the invocation created each path it removes.
forbid_1_consequence: A failure or signal can delete predecessor or concurrent state.
forbid_2_pattern: mv -n .*signed-exec.pending.*signed-exec
forbid_2_reason: Without -T, an existing destination directory is a target directory rather than a no-replace publication conflict.
forbid_2_consequence: The owned pending tree is nested inside and mutates the foreign destination.
